
schema Improvements;

/*

Note about AIAlignments:

They are optional, if you don't add them at all the AI system will attempt to fill them out from the data (mainly from buffs)

If there are partially filled out the AI system will attempt to fill out any unset values
Any entry filled out between -10 and +10 will be accepted and used directly
An entry that you want the AI to fill out (as opposed to the entire array) would have <byte>AIAlignment.AUTO_ALIGNMENT_VALUE for it's value

A fully filled out block will look something like this (this is random, I hope none actually use these values
.alignment = 
{
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Prestige]     = 5i8,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Research]     = 0i8,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Masterpieces] = 2i8,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Religion]     = 4i8,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Production]   = 6i8,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Offense]      = -8i8,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Defense]      = -8i8,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Food]         = 5i8,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Stone]        = 5i8,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Wood]         = 5i8,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Money]        = 5i8,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Happiness]    = 5i8,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Health]       = 5i8,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Wealth]       = 5i8,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Education]    = 5i8,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Security]     = 5i8,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Bias]         = 7i8,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Diplomacy]    = 0i8,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Housing]      = 5i8,
},

These values will essentially have a dot product taken with an aspect of game state (in the same format) to determine the best value
Note that if the game state has a negative on an element, then having a positve in the value for the improvement will make it less likely to be chosen

Bias doesn't map to anything in particular. It is a hammer that can be used to tell the AI that this is very good (or bad) as the corresponding gamestate
that it will be dotted against is will alwys be assumed to be +10.

If needed, more categories can be added.

I shorter version that also works would look like this:

.alignment = 
{
    // Prestige Research Masterpieces Religion Production Offense Defense Food Stone Wood Money Happiness Health Wealth Education Security Bias Diplomacy Housing
        0i8,     0i8,     0i8,         0i8,     4i8,       0i8,    0i8,    0i8, 0i8,  0i8, 0i8,  0i8,      0i8,   0i8,   0i8,      0i8,     0i8, 0i8,      0i8,
},

A partially filled out one will look something like this:

.alignment = update(defaultData.alignment)
{
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Bias] = 5i8,
},

This is the same thing as:

.alignment = 
{
 	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Prestige]     = <byte>AIAlignment.AUTO_ALIGNMENT_VALUE,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Research]     = <byte>AIAlignment.AUTO_ALIGNMENT_VALUE,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Masterpieces] = <byte>AIAlignment.AUTO_ALIGNMENT_VALUE,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Religion]     = <byte>AIAlignment.AUTO_ALIGNMENT_VALUE,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Production]   = <byte>AIAlignment.AUTO_ALIGNMENT_VALUE,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Offense]      = <byte>AIAlignment.AUTO_ALIGNMENT_VALUE,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Defense]      = <byte>AIAlignment.AUTO_ALIGNMENT_VALUE,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Food]         = <byte>AIAlignment.AUTO_ALIGNMENT_VALUE,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Stone]        = <byte>AIAlignment.AUTO_ALIGNMENT_VALUE,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Wood]         = <byte>AIAlignment.AUTO_ALIGNMENT_VALUE,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Money]        = <byte>AIAlignment.AUTO_ALIGNMENT_VALUE,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Happiness]    = <byte>AIAlignment.AUTO_ALIGNMENT_VALUE,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Health]       = <byte>AIAlignment.AUTO_ALIGNMENT_VALUE,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Wealth]       = <byte>AIAlignment.AUTO_ALIGNMENT_VALUE,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Education]    = <byte>AIAlignment.AUTO_ALIGNMENT_VALUE,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Security]     = <byte>AIAlignment.AUTO_ALIGNMENT_VALUE,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Bias]         = 5i8,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Diplomacy]    = <byte>AIAlignment.AUTO_ALIGNMENT_VALUE,
	[AIAlignment.Alignment.Housing]      = <byte>AIAlignment.AUTO_ALIGNMENT_VALUE,
},

In this case the update() is needed

*/

// this is needed to have autoAlignment work with partially filled out entries
ImprovementTemplate defaultData = {};

